index=<windows_index>
    sourcetype="WinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational"
    EventCode=4104
    ( "export-pfxcertificate" OR "export-certificate" OR "exportpfx"
      OR "X509ContentType" OR "crypto::capi" OR "crypto::certificates" )

``` Message field is not guaranteed depending on TA / XML ingest ```
| eval msg = replace(coalesce(Message, _raw), "[\r\n]+", " ")

``` Non-greedy with an end-of-string fallback: a truncated or trailer-less
    event degrades to a partial match instead of being silently dropped ```
| rex field=msg "Creating Scriptblock text \((?<sb_part>\d+) of (?<sb_total>\d+)\):(?<command_executed>.*?)(?:ScriptBlock ID:\s*(?<scriptblock_id>[0-9A-Fa-f\-]+)|$)"
| eval command_executed = coalesce(command_executed, msg)
| where isnotnull(command_executed) AND command_executed != ""

``` Normalize trivial obfuscation before pattern matching.
    Strips backticks, quotes, carets. Does NOT defeat concatenation or
    IEX-wrapped encoding - see hunt notes at bottom. ```
| eval cmd_norm = lower(replace(command_executed, "[`'\"\^]", ""))

``` --------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Detection vector classification
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
| eval detection_method = case(
    match(cmd_norm, "crypto::(capi|certificates)"),
        "Mimikatz: crypto module",
    match(cmd_norm, "certutil") AND match(cmd_norm, "-?exportpfx"),
        "CertUtil: -exportPFX",
    match(cmd_norm, "export-pfxcertificate"),
        "PowerShell: Export-PfxCertificate",
    match(cmd_norm, "\.export\(") AND match(cmd_norm, "pfx|pkcs12"),
        ".NET: X509Certificate2.Export() - PFX",
    match(cmd_norm, "x509contenttype"),
        ".NET: X509ContentType reference",
    match(cmd_norm, "export-certificate"),
        "PowerShell: Export-Certificate (public key only)",
    true(),
        "Certificate Export: Unknown Vector"
)

``` --------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Scoring - derived from detection_method so the two can never disagree.
    Private-key material scores above public-key-only operations.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
| eval risk_score = case(
    detection_method=="Mimikatz: crypto module",                        95,
    detection_method=="CertUtil: -exportPFX",                           90,
    detection_method=="PowerShell: Export-PfxCertificate",              85,
    detection_method==".NET: X509Certificate2.Export() - PFX",          85,
    detection_method==".NET: X509ContentType reference",                75,
    detection_method=="PowerShell: Export-Certificate (public key only)", 60,
    true(),                                                             50
)

``` Escalate if the export is paired with a plaintext password or a
    write to a network / removable path - strong exfil indicator ```
| eval risk_score = case(
    match(cmd_norm, "convertto-securestring.*-asplaintext"), risk_score + 5,
    match(cmd_norm, "filepath\s*=?\s*\\\\\\\\"),             risk_score + 5,
    true(), risk_score
)
| eval risk_score = min(risk_score, 100)

| eval severity = case(
    risk_score >= 90, "Critical",
    risk_score >= 80, "High",
    risk_score >= 65, "Medium",
    true(),           "Low"
)

``` --------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Identity resolution - User is frequently empty on 4104
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
| eval actor = coalesce(user, User, UserID, "UNRESOLVED")

``` --------------------------------------------------------------------------
    TUNING - populate from your PKI / cert-automation inventory before enabling
    Known benign: win-acme, Posh-ACME, IIS renewal, SCCM/Intune, PKI admin hosts
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` | search NOT (host IN ("PKI-01","PKI-02") AND actor IN ("SVC_CERTRENEW")) ```
``` | search NOT match(cmd_norm, "posh-acme|win-acme|wacs\.exe") ```

| fillnull value="N/A" actor scriptblock_id
| table _time host actor EventCode severity risk_score detection_method
        scriptblock_id sb_part sb_total command_executed
| sort 0 -risk_score, -_time


``` ============================================================================
    SEARCH 2 of 2: PowerShell Module / Pipeline Logging (EventCode 4103)
    Run this SEPARATELY. 4103 has a completely different message structure -
    it cannot share the 4104 rex. This is the search that recovers the
    coverage the original query only appeared to have.
    ============================================================================ ```

index=<windows_index>
    sourcetype="WinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational"
    EventCode=4103
    ( "Export-PfxCertificate" OR "Export-Certificate" OR "certutil" )

| eval msg = replace(coalesce(Message, _raw), "[\r\n]+", " ")

``` 4103 exposes the resolved cmdlet name and bound parameters directly -
    this is why it survives aliasing that 4104 string matching can miss ```
| rex max_match=0 field=msg "CommandInvocation\((?<invoked_command>[^\)]+)\)"
| rex max_match=0 field=msg "ParameterBinding\([^\)]+\):\s*name=\"(?<param_name>[^\"]+)\";\s*value=\"(?<param_value>[^\"]*)\""
| rex field=msg "Command Name\s*=\s*(?<command_name>[^\s]+)"
| rex field=msg "Host Name\s*=\s*(?<ps_host_app>[^\s]+)"
| rex field=msg "User\s*=\s*(?<ps_user>[^\s]+)"
| rex field=msg "Command Type\s*=\s*(?<command_type>[^\s]+)"

| where isnotnull(invoked_command) OR isnotnull(command_name)

| eval resolved = lower(coalesce(command_name, mvjoin(invoked_command, ",")))
| eval detection_method = case(
    match(resolved, "export-pfxcertificate"), "PowerShell: Export-PfxCertificate (module log)",
    match(resolved, "export-certificate"),    "PowerShell: Export-Certificate (module log)",
    match(resolved, "certutil"),              "CertUtil invoked from PowerShell",
    true(), "Certificate operation - review"
)
| eval risk_score = case(
    match(resolved, "export-pfxcertificate"), 85,
    match(resolved, "certutil"),              85,
    match(resolved, "export-certificate"),    60,
    true(), 50
)
| eval severity = case(
    risk_score >= 80, "High",
    risk_score >= 65, "Medium",
    true(), "Low"
)
| eval actor = coalesce(ps_user, user, User, "UNRESOLVED")

| fillnull value="N/A"
| table _time host actor EventCode severity risk_score detection_method
        command_name command_type ps_host_app param_name param_value
| sort 0 -risk_score, -_time


``` ============================================================================
    HUNT NOTES - coverage this pair still does NOT provide
    ============================================================================

    1. certutil.exe run OUTSIDE PowerShell.
       Requires process-creation telemetry, not the PowerShell log:
         EventCode=4688 OR (sourcetype=Sysmon EventCode=1)
         Image="*\\certutil.exe" CommandLine="*exportPFX*"
       Also cover the store-enumeration precursor: certutil -store my

    2. AD CS abuse (ESC1-ESC8 / Certipy / Certify.exe).
       Higher-impact T1649 path. Lives in the CA event log:
         sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode IN (4886, 4887, 4899, 4900)
       Watch for requests where SAN != requesting principal.

    3. PFX/P12 file artifacts on disk.
         Sysmon EventCode=11 TargetFilename IN ("*.pfx","*.p12")
       Correlate to the export event by host + 60s window. Catches the
       .NET Export() path even when the script block itself is obfuscated.

    4. Obfuscation this does not defeat.
       String concatenation ("Export-Pfx"+"Certificate"), -EncodedCommand,
       and IEX-wrapped payloads. Add a companion hunt on 4104 for:
         base64 blobs > 500 chars, FromBase64String, high-entropy strings,
         and concatenation density (count of "+" adjacent to quoted fragments).

    5. Non-exportable key theft via DPAPI.
       If the private key is flagged non-exportable, actors pivot to CAPI/CNG
       key blobs in %APPDATA%\Microsoft\Crypto\* and DPAPI masterkeys.
       Mimikatz crypto::capi / crypto::cng. Monitor file reads on those paths.

    ============================================================================
    KNOWN LIMITATION - script block fragmentation
    ============================================================================
    A single script logs as N sequential 4104 events ("1 of 3", "2 of 3"...).
    Because the search filters on the keyword, only the fragment containing
    the keyword is returned - command_executed may be a partial command.
    For IR-grade reassembly, take the scriptblock_id from an alert and run:

      index=<windows_index> EventCode=4104 ScriptBlockId="<guid>"
      | rex field=_raw "Creating Scriptblock text \((?<p>\d+) of (?<t>\d+)\):(?<txt>.*?)ScriptBlock ID:"
      | sort 0 +p
      | stats list(txt) as parts by ScriptBlockId
      | eval full_script = mvjoin(parts, "")
    ============================================================================ ```
